diff --git a/docs/sop-verification-mvp.md b/docs/sop-verification-mvp.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0495b57
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/sop-verification-mvp.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Task SOP verification MVP
+
+This adds explicitly requested candidate reports, independently of TaskCheck and Finish Gate. It does not activate knowledge, record a human check, complete a task or change a project SOP.
+
+## API contract
+
+- `POST /api/v1/projects/{project}/tasks/{task}/sop-verifications`: browser cookie and CSRF, existing Task edit permission. Body: `{"sop_version":1,"target_commit":"optional full 40-character SHA"}`. No uploaded candidate, source text, model settings or token scope is accepted. The user must be told that selected materials are sent to DeepSeek.
+- `GET` the same path with `limit=25&offset=0`: project read permission, returns `{items,total,next_offset}`. Items contain only IDs, author/time, status, exact SOP pin, input digest and result/count metadata. A withdrawn SOP or revoked source can still have metadata in this history; its frozen body remains access-controlled.
+- `GET /.../sop-verifications/{id}`: checks current project/source access and that the pinned SOP remains active. Returns metadata plus `input_snapshot`, `scope_snapshot`, `source_refs_by_id` and the original worker `report`.
+
+`POST` returns 201 after appending a report. Status `candidate` means the candidate analysis completed; `failed` preserves an incomplete analysis. Provider failures leave all four conditions unknown; individual candidate-validation failures may preserve other valid conditions. A completed provider request can still produce a failed analysis. Neither status means formal approval. Missing configuration returns 503, malformed worker output 502, worker timeout 504, input overflow 413, and incomplete target diff 409. Worker crashes/timeouts do not append a report. No report-update/delete API exists.
+
+## Frozen evidence
+
+Only the Task's explicit `source_bindings` are read; `session_ids` alone are not a selection. Open `session_from` bindings resolve to a fixed turn list for that report. All pages of normalized visible events are read, including the middle of long tool results. A selected unreadable source fails the request; it is never skipped. The limit is 400 sources, 320,000 source characters and 2 MiB stdin; larger scopes are rejected without truncation.
+
+The scope keeps physical source locations, original Task fields, capture status and time. The existing visible-event adapter excludes system/meta/sidechain/compact-summary records. Reading every selected page does not prove every real-world action was captured. Partial/unknown capture is sent as `evidence_completeness: partial`; the worker must downgrade positive conclusions while retaining supported failures and gaps. Current permissions and source locations are fenced again before insertion. A Task or source that changes during analysis requires a new request.
+
+An optional target SHA must already belong to this project. The existing Git diff reader is used only after authorizing its exact selected connection. Whole/file truncation, binary data and missing patches are rejected. The complete diff is frozen with `version_id` and a Server-created manual locator. Without a target, change-coverage conditions remain unknown.
+
+The exact SOP bundle is checked with the existing RFC 8785 digest implementation. Reports keep the original worker output. Model evidence IDs/line ranges/quotes are checked against the frozen input; UI source links must use Server-created `source_refs_by_id`, not model-supplied locators.
+
+## Runtime
+
+Configure absolute `FORMSY_SOP_VERIFICATION_PYTHON` and `FORMSY_SOP_VERIFICATION_WORKER` paths. Leave them empty to disable triggering. The standalone worker entry is `scripts/verify.py` in the separate `formsy-sop-verification` repository. It uses Python standard-library dependencies and is invoked directly as `python -I /absolute/scripts/verify.py`, without a shell, arbitrary executable arguments, inherited process environment or stderr capture. It has 120 seconds, 1 MiB stdout and two concurrent slots per Server process.
+
+`FORMSY_SOP_VERIFICATION_MODEL` defaults to `deepseek-flash`. `FORMSY_SOP_VERIFICATION_API_KEY_REF` defaults to `env://DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`; it may explicitly reference an already deployed secret such as `env://FORMSY_KNOWLEDGE_MODEL_API_KEY`. The Server resolves that reference and passes only `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` and the chosen model to the child. No `.env` file, credentials or private report history is copied into the worker repository.
+
+The API image includes Python. To mount a deployed worker checkout read-only, set the absolute `FORMSY_SOP_VERIFICATION_REPO` and use `docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.sop-verification.yaml ...`. Provision the key using the existing deployment secret process. Reverse proxies must allow a response timeout above 120 seconds (150 seconds recommended); the Web request timeout is 180 seconds. This synchronous small-scope MVP does not add a background queue.
+
+## Verification
+
+Focused Server tests cover Task permissions/CSRF, exact/withdrawn SOPs, immutable rounds, history paging, complete long-tool pagination, capture gaps, overflow, failed model rounds, quote boundaries, complete target diffs and absence of TaskCheck/completion writes. An optional cross-repository smoke uses the actual worker entrypoint with synthetic offline material, never a real model:
+
+```
+FORMSY_TEST_SOP_WORKER=/absolute/formsy-sop-verification/scripts/verify.py \
+cargo test -p formsy-server --lib deployed_worker_contract_smoke -- --ignored --test-threads=1
+```
+
+The worker's four-condition draft mapping is partial coverage of the six SOP chapters. Tests, a model candidate, human review and production deployment are separate evidence states.
